# Automation server — agent access and deploy

## SSH (from dev PC / Cursor agent)

| Item | Value |
|------|--------|
| Host | `192.168.2.4` |
| User | `tinel` |
| Key | `%USERPROFILE%\.ssh\serverside_192_168_2_4_ed25519` (Windows) or `~/.ssh/serverside_192_168_2_4_ed25519` |
| Optional alias | `serverside` (see `scripts/server/ssh_config.snippet`) |

**Agent remote command template (single line):**

`ssh -o BatchMode=yes -i %USERPROFILE%\.ssh\serverside_192_168_2_4_ed25519 tinel@192.168.2.4 "<command>"`

Key auth was verified with `BatchMode=yes`. Do not use password SSH or scp for routine deploys.

## Sudo for agent (user runs on server once per session)

`sed -i 's/\r$//' /opt/dell_server_management/scripts/server/*.sh && cd /opt/dell_server_management && sudo ./scripts/server/grant_temporary_agent_sudo.sh`

Verify: `bash /opt/dell_server_management/scripts/server/check_deploy_sudo.sh` → expect `sudo-n: ok` / `mode: agent`.

Agent uses `sudo -n` over SSH after grant. Never ask user to run PowerShell SSH setup scripts.

## Deploy files — git only (not scp)

1. **Dev machine:** commit and `git push` changes to the remote.
2. **Server git checkout:** `ssh … "cd ~/ServerBootShutdownManagemement && git fetch && git checkout <branch> && git pull"`
3. **Apply to production tree:** `ssh … "cd ~/ServerBootShutdownManagemement && printf '\n' | sudo ./update.sh"`  
   (`update.sh` copies repo → `/opt/dell_server_management`, preserves config, restarts services.)
4. **Verify install scripts:** after `update.sh`, run targeted installers if needed, e.g.  
   `ssh … "cd /opt/dell_server_management && sudo -n bash ./install_energy_consumers_service.sh"`

| Path | Role |
|------|------|
| `~/ServerBootShutdownManagemement` | Git working copy on server (pull here) |
| `/opt/dell_server_management` | Production install (`update.sh` target) |

**Do not** copy trees with `scp` except emergency hotfix; always prefer commit → push → pull → `update.sh`.

Fresh install or rebuild: `sudo ./install.sh` from pulled repo (rare; preserves `.env` backups).

## Post-deploy checks (single lines)

`ssh … "systemctl is-active energy-consumers-publisher.service victron-mqtt-publisher.service huawei-mqtt-publisher.service"`

`ssh … "timeout 35 mosquitto_sub -h localhost -t 'energy/consumers/+/status' -C 1 -v"`

Node-RED flows: generate/deploy from dev PC via `nodered/live-connection/scripts/` (uses `NODE_RED_BASE_URL` in `.env`).

Full reference: `docs/developer/SERVER_DEPLOY.md`, `scripts/server/README.md`.
